-- title:
--   Degree of composita: [C ι'(E'):C ι(E)]≤[E':E]
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $E$ and $E'$ be fields that are $k$-algebras, with $E'$ an $E$-algebra forming a scalar tower over $k$ and with $E'$ finite as an $E$-module; let $C$ and $\Omega$ be fields with $C$ a $k$-algebra, $\Omega$ a $C$-algebra and a $k$-algebra, again forming a scalar tower. Let $\iota\colon E\to\Omega$ and $\iota'\colon E'\to\Omega$ be ring homomorphisms (no compatibility with the $k$-structures is required) such that $\iota'(\,\cdot\,)$ restricted along the structure map $E\to E'$ equals $\iota$, i.e. $\iota'(\mathrm{algebraMap}_{E,E'}(x))=\iota(x)$ for all $x\in E$. Write $A$ for the subfield of $\Omega$ generated by the image of $C$ together with $\iota(E)$, and $B$ for the subfield generated by the image of $C$ together with $\iota'(E')$. Then the relative degree `Subfield.relfinrank` $A\,B$, that is the $\Omega$-dimension count $\operatorname{finrank}_{A\sqcap B}B$, is at most $\operatorname{finrank}_E E'$. Since $\iota(E)\subseteq\iota'(E')$ one has $A\le B$, so the conclusion reads $[\,C\,\iota'(E') : C\,\iota(E)\,]\le[E':E]$.
--
--   This is the standard estimate that forming a compositum with a fixed field $C$ inside an ambient field $\Omega$ cannot increase a finite degree: the degree of $C\,\iota'(E')$ over $C\,\iota(E)$ is bounded by $[E':E]$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd descent arguments, in the two lemmas producing an intertwining operator from base data, where a bound on the degree of a generated subfield is needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Subfield_relfinrank_closure_le_finrank_of_comp.lean

